## Why This Is Asked
Tests branchless 128-bit rotation using only shifts.

## Key Concepts
- View 128-bit value via 128-bit type
- Branchless rotation with shifts and modulo
- Correct unpacking into hi/lo

## Code Example
```c
void rotateRight128(uint64_t hi, uint64_t lo, unsigned int k, uint64_t *out_hi, uint64_t *out_lo) {
  unsigned int kk = k & 127;
  __uint128_t v = (((__uint128_t)hi) << 64) | lo;
  v = (v >> kk) | (v << ((128 - kk) % 128));
  *out_hi = (uint64_t)(v >> 64);
  *out_lo = (uint64_t)v;
}
```

